From: Arsslen Idadi <arsslens021@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:12:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] focaltech_moh: match with the minutiae matcher, in a
 thread

Verify and identify now go through focaltech_moh_match.c, and share one
state machine. A probe that is not usable is a retry, asking to centre the
finger, not a failed attempt. Prints of the earlier format are not read;
their fingers must be enrolled again.

Enrolment keeps every usable press, with the earlier presses it links to:
aligned at NCC >= 0.5 with at least two more minutiae paired than unpaired.
Presses linked together, directly or through others, show one finger;
enrolment is as far along as the largest such group, and ends once it holds
15. A press of another finger never joins that group, and neither does a
first press the following ones do not overlap, which would otherwise hold
the whole enrolment hostage. At most 24 presses are kept; when full, those
outside the largest group make room.

Making a press ready and comparing it takes a good fraction of a second, so
it runs in a GTask thread, as minutiae detection does for image devices,
and the main loop does not stall.

The 2808:9338 test was recorded with flat skin rather than a fingertip, so
that it carries no fingerprint. The matcher needs ridges and rightly enrols
nothing from it, so the test now captures a frame and checks the protocol;
matching is covered by test-focaltech-moh-match.
